The Fourier-based azimuthal kernel provides the capability to capture the flow physics based on our understanding of the rotor wake. It incorporates the periodic nature of a rotating blade due to its sinusoidal nature. The wave numbers defined by the kernel correspond to the n/rev components that exist within a rotor wake. For a two-bladed rotor, a dominant 2/rev component as well as weaker higher even harmonics are expected.
