SUMMARY AND CONCLUSIONS
This work describes two parallel approaches to estimate rotor thrust from non-contact measurements: an aerodynamics approach and a structural dynamics approach. In the aerodynamic approach, flow fields measured from timeresolved PIV were used to train a Gaussian Process model. A higher-fidelity flow field was then generated by the model, that included radial and azimuthal locations not covered by the PIV measurements. The model also reduced measurement noise and filled in missing data where PIV measurements were not successful, such as in tip vortex cores, regions with laser light reflections from the rotor
